{title: Road to Damascus}
{subtitle: Acts 9:1–9; 9:17–18}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [B] | [F#] | [C#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I was [D#m]breathing out threats against the church of the Way
[B]Letters from the high priest, chains for those who pray
On [F#]the road to Damascus, noon, the sun overhead
A light [C#]from heaven flashed and I fell like the dead
[D#m]Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me
Who [B]are you, Lord, tell me who I'm meant to see
I [F#]am Jesus, the one you have been fighting
[C#]Get up, go to the city, you'll be told what is right
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On [D#m]the road to Damascus I was [B]blind
But [F#]I saw the light for the first [C#]time
Scales [D#m]fell from my [B]eyes
Now I walk [F#]the road of [C#]life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Three days I [D#m]sat in the dark, no food, no drink
[B]Couldn't see a thing, all I could do was think
[F#]Then Ananias came and laid his hands on me
Broth[C#]er Saul, the Lord has sent me so you can see
Something [D#m]like scales fell off and I rose
Baptized in the [B]name I had fought, now I know
The one I perse[F#]cuted is the one who called my name
Chief of sinners, saved by [C#]grace, never the same
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the [D#m]road to Damascus I was [B]blind
But [F#]I saw the light for the first [C#]time
Scales [D#m]fell from my [B]eyes
Now I walk [F#]the road of [C#]life
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [C#] | [D#m] | [B] | [F#] |
| [C#] |
